<title>EGYPT: Egypt pound interbank rates rise.</title>
<headline>Egypt pound interbank rates rise.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound rose in a balanced private-sector market on Sunday to between 7-1/2 and 8-3/4 percent from Thursday's range of seven and 8-1/4 percent, bankers said.</p>
<p>One-week rates also rose to between eight and nine percent from seven and eight percent on Thursday, they added.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is neutral. There are offerings and there is demand,&quot; one banker told Reuters.</p>
<p>The public sector retained its lending rate at 10-1/2 percent.</p>
<p>$1=3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
